{
    // VANILLA
    "Strings.HailAndWellMet": "Do not abandon Hope, for she is infinite, and unwilling to stand by in the presence of Evil.",
    // ARTIFICER HOUSE
    "Strings.PepperRexBed": "There seems to be a heating pad underneath the hay.",
    "Strings.QuackQuestion": "A very dapper duck; it was previously Val's.",
    "Strings.EmeritusToys": "None of these look as well-loved as the duckie.",
    "Strings.CiderKeg": "A keg of mulled cider spiked with a cinnamon-flavored whiskey.",
    "Strings.LiquorCabinet": "A collection of vintage liquors of varying types.",
    "Strings.Kegarator": "The tap on the left pours a fruited sour, the tap on the right pours a chocolate stout.",
    "Strings.LynchCoffeeMaker": "%This espresso maker is unusual looking, but brews a damn fine cup of coffee.",
    "Strings.ValFridge": "There's a magnet of a Pepper Rex and a photograph of a Stygium vein.",
    "Strings.OldEspresso": "This stovetop espresso maker is battered, clearly a hand-me-down.",
    "Strings.TwedesCoffee": "The label on the coffee bag reads 'Twede's Cafe'.",
    "Strings.ValDesk": "Val's desk is very organized; it appears they're trying to map out Deep Dark levels.",
    "Strings.ParchmentSkeleton": "The little plaque at the bottom of this standee reads 'Parchment: He's got a bone to pick with you.'",
    "Strings.DoctorVal": "A doctorate in Metallurgical Engineering issued to Valene M. Luis.",
    "Strings.GeoffTheLandshark": "A plush shark with a tag that reads 'Geoff'. He's very squished, and a little dirty; to love is to be changed.",
    "Strings.StygiumSword": "A poisonous blade sounds advantageous in theory, but Stygium is so infectious it may backfire on the wielder.",
    "Strings.StygiumSkull": "The creature skill in this case has taken on a strange hue, and it seems to be growing small crystals.",
    "Strings.StygiumShield": "This small buckler may have been paired with the sword. Wearing a bracer underneath might have slowed the rate of corruption.",
    "Strings.StygiumVase": "This vase isn't well-made; it was likely an early attempt at crafting with Stygium.",
    "Strings.StygiumPlant": "Once green, this plant seems to have been impacted by the nearby Stygium. No wonder everything's behind glass now...",
    "Strings.ValBooks1": "While one shelf is dedicated to textbooks, the rest is all fiction. In particular, there's a well-loved copy of 'The Great Gatsbish'.",
    "Strings.ValBooks2": "This entire bookshelf is packed to the brim with tabletop supplements for different games.",
    "Strings.ArtifactShelf": "Recreations of macguffins from various movies and books, all neatly displayed.",
    "Strings.DiceChest": "An entire treasure chest's worth of dice.",
    "Strings.PonderingOrb": "For pondering, of course.",
    "Strings.TabletopSession": "Val's game is about an expedition of adventurers delving into the winding unknown, lower and lower until the only thing left to face is themselves.",
    "Strings.SenRoom": "A storage room. There's nothing of interest back here.",
    "Strings.LavaTresspass": "Beware: Lava!",
    "Strings.HandpaintedSign": "Val crafted this sign by hand. The lettering reads: 'The Underforge'.",
    "Strings.Underforge": "Val's unusual forge, powered by lava and cooled by water.",
    "Strings.ValAnvil": "Val's anvil is old, but well cared for. It sees a lot of use.",
    "Strings.MoatToNowhere": "You're not entirely sure where this water runs out toward.",
    "Strings.CritterRoom": "You could've sworn you heard something behind the wall...",
    "Strings.ValToDo": "An extensive to-do list. There are notes, tasks, dates, and reminders.",
    "Strings.WhyBoat": "The purpose of this boat eludes even your most sharpened guesses.",
    "Strings.GreenLight": "Gatsbish believed in the green light, the orgastic future that year by year recedes before us. It eluded us then, but that's no matter— tomorrow we will run faster, stretch out our arms farther.... And one fine morning— So we beat on, boats against the current, borne back ceaselessly into the past.",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.1": "A record spins before you...:# 'I can feel the thunder that's breaking in your heart, I can see through the scars inside you...!'",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.2": "A record spins before you...:# 'It's the cruel beast that you feed, it's your burning yearning need to bleed through the spillways...!'",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.3": "A record spins before you...:# 'The bringer of night, now and for always... a perpetual rise, a fall of illusion...#Your zenith fades into eternity, time will soon be gone...!'",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.4": "A record spins before you...:# 'I don't want my fangs too long...#If you have Ghost, you have everything...!'",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.5": "A record spins before you...:# 'The world is on fire, and you are here to stay and burn with me... our funeral pyre!'",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.6": "A record spins before you...:# 'Ripping through every poem, like a vampire should...#and it takes one to know 'em, like I knew you would...!'",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.7": "A record spins before you...:# 'I don't wanna end like this...#but the sting in the way you kiss me, something within your eyes...!'",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.8": "A record spins before you...:# 'And after all the sorrow, we'll be riding high...#And the truth of the matter is, I'll never let you go, let you go...!'",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.9": "A record spins before you...:# 'Love rockets! Shot right in between your eyes...#Love rockets! Excite me with your demise...'",
    "Strings.GhastRadio.10": "A record spins before you...:# 'I should have known not to give in... Blasphemy, heresy!#Save me from the monster that is eating me, I'm victimized...!'",
    // BARD HOUSE
    "Strings.ScatteredSheetMusic": "The sheet music on the table is a work in progress; of note, there is a napkin with manically scrawled lyrics in tight handwriting.",
    "Strings.MusicTheory": "A book on evoking specific feelings through specific melodies.",
    "Strings.MusicTheory2": "A book on poignant word usage in song lyrics.",
    "Strings.IncrediWomanComics": "In between records, playbills, and trinkets acquired from travel, there are tons of IncrediWoman comic books and novelizations.",
    "Strings.BigPiano": "The piano is a bit battered, as if it's come along on multiple moves. Otherwise, it's well taken care of, and accented adorably.",
    "Strings.MusicProductionStation": "This workstation seems top of the line; Coriander used what industry connections she had to bring some gear home with her.",
    "Strings.StageOutfit": "Coriander's stage outfit. A leather jumpsuit with metal accessories, including a helmet with a light-up emotive screen. It was her entire brand.",
    "Strings.GrammyAward": "An award for Best Song, won the year before Coriander returned to East Scarp.",
    "Strings.CoriPlant1": "Coriander expected this plant to stay a lot smaller.",
    "Strings.CoriPlant2": "A basket of cozy sweaters.",
    "Strings.CoriPlant3": "There's a note in the planter that reads: 'I hope this starter grows! Take good care of it. Love, Mom.'",
    "Strings.CoriPlant4": "Cori's favorite mug. It seems plain until you turn it around; not only is it handmade, but the signature carved underneath says 'Made by Mom, with all the love I can give.'",
    "Strings.CoriPlant5": "This one is plastic... but there's freshly watered dirt in the planter.",
    "Strings.CoriPlant6": "Being higher up and close to the telescope dome does these plants very well.",
    "Strings.TinyChica": "A weird chicken action figure guards Coriander's watering can. Is it's beak broken?",
    "Strings.TinyFreddy": "Coriander's favorite chair, taken up by one of many toys from Bobby Bearclaw's.",
    "Strings.TinyBonnie": "Cori's Gamestation 2. One of her many Bobby Bearclaw figures guards her surprisingly extensive game collection. She seems to enjoy RPGs and platformers.",
    "Strings.MeteorCollection": "Little notes frame each meteorite. They come from all over, but they all look relatively similar...",
    "Strings.AstrologyBooks": "There's a book or two on astrology, but they don't seem to have been touched in a while. The ones with a lot of wear are all textbooks covering cosmology, planetary science, and astrobiology.",
    "Strings.StygiumIsFromSpace": "This is supposedly another meteorite, but it looks more like Stygium.",
    "Strings.CoriKitchen": "The space is a little cluttered, but not unclean.",
    "Strings.BigFreddy": "A ginormous Bobby Bearclaw. He's very well loved; and nearly as old as Coriander.",
    "Strings.BigTelescope": "Coriander's telescope has seen a ton of use, but it's kept in immaculate condition.",
    "Strings.CoriPosters": "Posters, lovingly framed. Coriander's biggest inspirations...",
    "Strings.CoriGramophone": "The record on the label just says 'Stan'.",
    "Strings.SophieHat": "Made by a Hatter all the way in the Kingdom of Ingary, acquired while touring.",
    "Strings.CoriGuitar": "Ol' reliable. Coriander's first instrument, still occasionally used.",
    "Strings.MothersLetters": "There are letters tucked behind these framed canvases, signed by - who you can assume to be - Coriander's mother. Apparently she's in rehab, where these were all painted.",
    "Strings.WillysWonderland": "A pinball machine with a cast of characters similar to the Bobby Bearclaw ones, called 'Willy's Wonderland'. Coriander's high score is absurd.",
    "Strings.PolybiusCabinet": "Staring at this arcade cabinet for too long makes you feel a little woozy...",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.1": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'Why can't you see, what you're doing to me, when you don't believe a word I say... We can't go on together with suspicious minds!'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.2": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'You ain't nothin' but a hound dog, just crying all the time. Well, you ain't never caught no rabbit, and you ain't no friend of mine. Well, they said you was high-classed, well, that was just a lie.'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.3": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'You're the cutest jailbird I ever did see, I sure would be delighted with your company - Come on and do the Jailhouse Rock with me!'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.4": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'Is this the real life? Is this just fantasy? Caught in a landslide, no escape from reality. Open your eyes, look up to the skies and see...'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.5": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'I see a little silhouetto of a man! Scaramouche, scaramouche, will you do the fandango? Thunderbolt and lightening, very very frightening me-!'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.6": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'I will be king, and you, you will be queen. Though nothing will drive them away, we can beat them, just for one day. We can be heroes, just for one day.'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.7": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'This is Major Tom to Ground Control, I'm stepping through the door and I'm floating in a most peculiar way, and the stars look very different today...'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.8": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'If you say run, I'll run with you. And if you say hide, we'll hide, because my love for you would break my heart in two. If you should fall into my arms, and tremble like a flower, let's dance!'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.9": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'Autumn winds blowing outside the window as I look outside the room, and it makes me so depressed to see the gloom. There's not a soul out there, no one to hear my prayer...'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.10": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'Don't go wasting your emotion... Lay all your love on me! Don't go sharing your devotion... Lay all your love on me!'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.11": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'You better lose yourself in the music, the moment, you own it, you better never let it go! You only get one shot, do not miss your chance to blow, this opportunity comes once in a lifetime, yo!'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.12": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'My tea's gone cold, I'm wondering why, I got out of bed at all. The morning rain clouds up my window, and I can't see at all... and even if I could it'd all be gray. But your picture on my wall... it reminds me that it's not so bad, it's not so bad...'",
    "Strings.PostmodernJukebox.13": "You play a sick tune on the Jukebox...:# 'I hope you get to read this letter, I just hope it reaches you in time, before you hurt yourself, I think that you'll be doin' just fine. If you relax a little, I'm glad I inspire you, but, Stan - Why are you so mad? Try to understand that I do want you as a fan, I just don't want you to do some crazy shit...'",
}